  "changes": [
    "Ownership-consuming BASIC search entrypoints can select private storage only after whole-graph empty/known-node/exact builtin ID/key/payload/score preflight. Unsupported/populated/activity/batched graphs fall back before activation. Public directors, retained and monitored manager/service paths keep ordinary storage. No graph escapes through provider/observer/results.",
    "Private terminals retain copied IDs and contribution scores instead of payload owners. Every callback, structural check, old/new score clone, checked adjustment and final ID/payload clone phase remains. Full/current/nested captures, metrics and ordered diagnostic equality retain their logical state.",
    "Certified private planning sources copy rows and journal preimages/current/full captures by value, including573 rows. Cold source inspection can materialize a disposable map, but captures never promote row owners. Public source storage and prior fixed-source limits remain unchanged.",
    "Certified consuming joins can copy bounded ordinal input payloads in FixedRows while keeping canonical input ID Arcs and FixedIndex unchanged. Complete original <=4096 binding and exact primitive payload certificates apply; unbound member joins and custom/public standalone paths keep shared rows. First-preimage nested journals and saved candidates preserve rollback.",
    "Fixed primitive equality joins traverse bucket words directly after the same lookup and full output reservation. Canonical ascending input IDs, retractions/puts, projection and output Clone/Drop/panic phases and poisoned installation remain. This removes composite iterator construction/copies; custom keys and inequalities retain their original route."
  ],
  "tradeoffs": [
    "Copied terminal/source/join snapshots use more bytes than shared pointer arrays and terminal full captures sort sparse positions. Candidate captures retain only touched positions; no universal memory or code-size improvement is claimed.",
    "Internal ownership may differ only inside the certified consuming scope. No callback purity follows from NoDrop; user callbacks still run for every original event. Public retained graph match/snapshot owners remain unchanged.",
    "No application model, fixture, runtime settings, batch policy, compiler target CPU, panic policy or runner changes. General fat LTO remains. Quality and feasibility remain separate without identical scores/traces.",
    "Small/mixed event experiments were not integrated. Prior cloned-preimage owned collector variants regressed sailing and were not repeated. Separate constituent sessions do not isolate component speedups; use the selected combined diagnostic or actual default qualifier for their respective claims."
  ],
